Note that, for $k$-colorings $f$ and $g$ of an induced subgraph of $G$, 
$\xb_f = \xb_g$ if and only if $g$ is obtained from $f$ by permuting colors.
It is easy to see that $f \sim_k g$ if $g$ is obtained from $f$ by permuting colors.
In this paper, we identify $f$ and $g$ if $g$ is obtained from $f$ by permuting colors.
