A workable hard subfamily exists, but only after tightening the task to a bounded certificate. I’m using the standard NP-complete “Kempe Distance on stars” reduction: a Hamiltonian cycle in a cubic graph expands to a short, replayable Kempe sequence, while the number of colors grows with the instance (avoiding the star-case FPT result). The witness can be a compact cycle that the verifier deterministically expands and replays, so it remains exact without demanding thousands of move lines from the solver. I’m now testing whether the planted cubic distribution leaks the cycle to cheap heuristics.
